WEBVTT

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.420
This is the power of the legendary sorceress.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.000
I imagine this town will burn with the fires of hell.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:54.830
This is good.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:02:00.520
After this massive amount of destruction, people will recognize the existence of magic.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:07.740
And eventually, that power will let anyone access the world's inner-workings, without restriction.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.390
Humanity will further evolve.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.870
Yumiko-chan...

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.530
Damn it! What's going on?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.190
Morishita!

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.250
That idiot!

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.420
Koyomi!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.800
Hurry up and get away from here!

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.670
But... But Yumiko-chan is...

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.810
Don't space out! We're getting out of here!

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:41.970
Misa-san!

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.430
One hour after it began, the Akihabara fire shows no sign of relenting,

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.860
even with the firefighters' hard work.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.820
Breaking news! Mysterious fire in Akihabara!

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.820
Is the criminal doing it for fun?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.820
Or is it terrorism?

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.570
So it's finally begun...

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.200
What, exactly, happened?

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.830
Digitalis Flammalacia is returning to life.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.840
Digitalis?

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.030
That's right.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:16.620
She's a vile, dark mage who took the lives of over 100,000 men.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.630
She's using Yumiko's body now to fully revive herself.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.720
We have to hurry and save Yumiko-chan!

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.350
Yumiko is no longer Yumiko.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.740
Then what should we do?

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.680
There's nothing we can do but take her down.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.690
Take her down... You mean Yumiko-chan?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.570
I have a Code ready to do just that.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.830
Using it, we'll kick Digitalis into another world.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.270
If we do that,

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:49.460
we can break Digitalis's evil cycle of self-resurrection in this world.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.700
This is the only "best option" available to us!

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:57.750
We can't. We can't do that!

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.440
Then... Then Yumiko-chan...

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.730
Yumiko understands, too.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:08.790
She's strived to become a stronger Classical Mage than anyone else.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.920
I'm a moron, so I don't really get what's going on,

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.470
but I think it's weird.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:22.230
I think it's weird that we'd sacrifice Yumiko-chan so that we can survive.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:27.110
If Ichinose Yumiko Christina has become Digitalis and will do nothing but evil,

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.380
then don't you think that it's our job to stop her?

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.110
But... But...

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.820
Go home, Koyomi.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.620
There's nothing you can do here.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.820
I'm going to see Yumiko-chan again!

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:47.430
No.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:51.840
We promised to meet at the donut place at 6:30!

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.720
I'm going to bring her back home!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.190
Koyomi!

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.550
Ow...

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.610
Are you okay?

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:23.010
I'd worry if I left you alone, considering you can't even use your cell phone right.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.340
I'll go with you.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.340
You sure you don't have to go, Kaho?

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.260
I've already done enough this time,

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.100
so I thought I'd leave the rest to everyone else.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:40.430
And you said something strange, so I figured I should ask you about it.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.100
What's that?

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:48.370
Issue #1: You haven't actually prepared any Code that can "kick" Digitalis to another world.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.530
Issue #2: If you had such a Code,

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:56.230
you'd have had no reason to send me your amulet in the first place.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.370
You would have just fought Digitalis and been done with it.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.500
Am I wrong?

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.700
Good job.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.880
My mind's the sole good thing about me.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.690
I see.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.880
I only prepared one thing, a ghostscript of myself.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:17.890
Were you trying to die, in order to leave a ghostscript behind?

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.270
Why were you trying to sacrifice yourself?

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.680
I thought about which would be better,

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.270
my killing Yumiko or Yumiko killing me.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.390
Even if I killed Yumiko,

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.910
the Sorceress's Library would remain, necessitating another sacrifice in the future.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:38.790
So if Yumiko killed me, that'd be better, ending the Library's continuous cycle.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:45.300
With my ghostscript, it is true that I can kick Digitalis, along with Yumiko, to another world.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.290
And that's the one "best option"?

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:50.290
That's right.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.510
Say there is a heaven and hell.

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:59.120
Out of 10,000 people, if 9,999 could go to heaven,

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.300
I imagine you'd choose to be the one going to hell.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.450
I guess.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:14.620
I was happy you trusted me and gave me the job of amplifying your ghostscript.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.820
So I'm thinking of trusting our ace.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.040
You mean Soshiro?

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.760
She's a slow, klutzy crybaby.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.400
She can only use wash basin summoning magic.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.060
And normally, she just uselessly tags along, but...

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:34.340
She has a strange power in that, when everything's almost lost,

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:38.900
she can cross the only tightrope left, crying and stumbling all the while.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:43.240
So you should try trusting your #1 student, as well.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.270
This is...

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.220
I told you not to count me out.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.470
Are you okay, Yumiko-chan?

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.710
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:23.740
These are...

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.550
<i>Take this!</i>

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.280
my memories.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:35.940
The curse placed on your life is my greatest gift to you.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.450
My great-grandfather...

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:42.960
He's getting younger.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.580
Am I going back in time?

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.590
What is this?

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:52.600
These aren't my memories...

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.100
Digitalis, you have lost!

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.120
Unfortunately, Karl Cristbarth,

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.590
even should this body die, so long as the Sorceress's Library exists,

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:04.250
I'll return to life, using another body.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.730
I am eternal!

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:10.010
No. Someday, one of my descendants will break that cycle!

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:13.610
I shall seal the Sorceress's Library until then!

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:20.990
Be cursed, all who walk the Earth!

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:25.010
These are Digitalis's memories.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:26.730
That's right.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.210
I was oppressed because I was different from others.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.860
No one would stand up for me.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:36.010
That's why I cursed it all.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:40.520
You should understand it, as well... The pain of being alone...

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.210
Alone...

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.310
You've done well to come. My newest companion,

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.060
I welcome you.

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.060
I wonder if she won't talk to me anymore.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:01.650
I wanted to be as good a mage as Misa-san, but...

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.090
Don't worry.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:06.800
I don't think it matters, given that there's no such thing as a "mage" anyway.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:07.830
Yes, there is!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:11.620
God, I'm not sure if you believe that or if you're just really slow.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.590
Jeez...

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:20.260
The hamburger we had was really good.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:23.270
Younger Yumiko-chan was cute, too.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:29.890
She always saved me. She's an important friend to me.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:37.970
Next time, I won't let go. It's my turn to save her.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.650
Where might you two be going?

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:45.380
You are my greatest unknowns.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:48.630
It'd be helpful if you both left this city.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.660
You go ahead.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.130
But...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.050
Aren't you saving the stupid girl?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:54.850
Go!

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.770
Where are you going?

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:03.410
Hey, there. You're fighting me.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.690
Oh, you dodged it.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.470
Guibarthez...

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.330
I still owe you from six years ago.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.070
I'm going to pay you back now.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:25.820
There!

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:32.820
Nicely dispelled, as always. But how long will you last?

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:34.810
There!

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:38.330
There! There! There! There!

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.370
Looks like you're at your limit.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.020
What?

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.240
I should go now.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.780
Why did you get in my way?

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.990
It's been a while, Guibarthez.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.040
One hundred years...

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:17.690
You have memories of me?

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.520
Well, that makes things easier.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.800
Let's work together again.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:24.970
What is a mere ghostscript saying?

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.840
Who do you think brought you back?!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:28.810
Perish!

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:38.910
Guibarthez-

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.230
You looked away.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.490
It's past seven!

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.990
Where's the donut shop?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.840
Yumiko-chan!

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:02.730
You're okay?

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.550
I came to fulfill our promise.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:09.010
You're not Yumiko-chan?

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:12.710
I am Yumiko and Digitalis.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:16.010
Ichinose Yumiko Cristina is a part of me.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:20.560
Hey, it's late. Let's go home.

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:24.530
I cannot do that. This world must be covered in flame.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:27.030
Why? That's bad!

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:31.710
Morishita Koyomi, Ichinose Yumiko Cristina's friend.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.790
You would do well to leave this place.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:38.810
As long as the Library cries out in unrelenting terror,

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.290
I must fight.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.840
It's overwhelming.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:04.610
The worm that Kaho put on the net is self-replicating and infecting computers worldwide.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:16.060
It continues to amplify my power, even as a ghostscript.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:20.170
I have more power now than Guibarthez did six years ago.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:24.240
Come out. I know you're unhurt.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.020
Anehara Misa's ghostscript.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.490
Nice to meet you.

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:40.770
You won't just go down easy for me, will you?

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.270
Go ahead and see.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:46.780
You're right. Transform to swords, my Code!

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:53.580
You're good.

00:14:57.090 --> 00:15:00.490
Yumiko-chan? Yumiko-chan, where are you?

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.200
Yumiko-chan?

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.520
I'll insert a Code directly into your body!

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:39.050
That was dangerous.

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:42.200
I'd be dead if I weren't a ghostscript.

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:44.320
What did Yumiko do?

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.490
It was almost like she just disappeared...

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:47.580
jini!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:49.760
Yes, ma'am.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.920
Putting aside the fact that she constructed some Code and escaped...

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.310
There's nothing that shows she even constructed the Code of Swords.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.640
Why?

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:06.870
There's only one possibility that comes to mind...

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:08.860
A Code that stops time!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.200
That's right.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:21.150
A time-stopping Code would probably involve temporarily moving your body

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:24.410
to another world where time flows differently.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:25.920
That's how you're doing it.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.710
You've figured it out, Modern-Day mage.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.180
So what will you do?

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:31.830
There's one possibility.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:36.470
If I channel the time-stopping Code's reaction into stopping this very world...

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:40.260
Koyomi, who's part of this world,

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:42.480
will automatically transform the Code into a wash basin...

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.920
changing Yumiko's time-stopping Code, too...

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.310
allowing me to neutralize it!

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:51.820
I'll borrow the power of all CPUs.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.210
Here I go!

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:24.260
Now!

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:34.380
What?

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:36.540
I won't let you get away!

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:49.820
Let's end all of this.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:00.720
Yumiko-chan!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.580
I'm going to save you, okay?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.830
Just a little bit more...

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:27.090
Stop.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.770
Yumiko-chan?

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:34.340
Friend of Ichinose Yumiko Cristina, Morishita Koyomi, that's enough.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:38.330
This is wrong! It's definitely, definitely wrong!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.600
Let go of my hand. I'm an enemy to this world.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:48.960
That doesn't matter! I'll protect you!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.620
You're my friend!

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:54.860
I'm definitely, definitely going to protect you!

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:59.490
No matter who stands against me, even if it's Misa-san...

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:02.270
So don't give up!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.630
At this rate, you'll get sucked in, too.

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:08.370
I still won't let go.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:13.620
I'll never, ever let go of your hand, Yumiko-chan.

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:16.050
Watch out!

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:19.060
Soshiro-san.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.850
Damn it...

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:50.820
Soshiro-san, why are you okay?

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:52.480
Who knows?

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.460
Don't ask me to explain nutty situations.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.990
Yumiko-chan, are you okay?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:03.970
The reincarnation granted by the Sorceress's Library uses death as its trigger to activate.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.480
It's a reflexive magic.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:09.470
If you send me to the other world, Digitalis will never return.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.470
Now's your only chance.

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:13.600
Yumiko-chan, I'm getting mad at you!

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:22.810
But to live alongside a friend might not be that bad, either.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.280
Yumiko-chan.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:28.490
I won't forgive you. I won't ever forgive you!

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:35.190
All mankind's knowledge...

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:36.690
Right here...

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.220
And you guys...

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.830
No, Gary Huang.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:49.680
Anehara Misa!

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:52.190
You're coming over here.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.680
Let's go together.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:59.730
It'll grow on you. I don't think the other world is such a bad place.

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:05.700
I planned to go with Yumiko, but it looks like she wasn't that into me, after all.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.330
I guess I'll have to live with you instead.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.290
Let go! Let go of me!

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:16.960
Stay well, Koyomi, Yumiko, Soshiro...

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.000
Let go!

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:23.510
Don't forgot our promise.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:25.870
If I'm killed,

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:28.690
then I will come back.

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:34.370
You'll protect me until I grow old

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:36.710
and die peacefully someday.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.690
Yumiko-chan!

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:41.740
You're heavy...

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:47.080
How rude! I'm not heavy at all!

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.280
Yumiko-chan?

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.730
What is it?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.290
You really are Yumiko-chan!

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:59.370
What are you doing?

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:03.140
I'm so happy. I'm so happy!

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.060
Jeez.

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:09.300
I'm back, Koyomi.

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:11.980
Welcome back.

00:22:34.070 --> 00:22:35.580
Sorry for the wait.

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:38.280
All of you, eat up.

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:40.550
Right!

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:45.140
It's good!

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:53.540
This is the cooking that created that mage-killer.

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:56.140
Is it okay if I have more?

00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:57.910
Of course.

